# Performance & Scaling Security

## Rate Limiting

- Add rate limiting to **all** public endpoints
- Strict limits on auth: 5-10 req/min login, 3-5 req/hour registration and password reset
- Rate limit by user ID (authenticated) + IP (fallback) — not IP alone (bypassable via proxies)
- Return `X-RateLimit-*` headers for client self-throttling
- Implement exponential backoff after auth failures
- Use Redis-backed rate limiting for multi-instance deployments

## Caching Security

- Set `Cache-Control: no-store, private` for authenticated/sensitive responses
- **Never** cache responses containing auth tokens, PII, or session data in shared caches
- Include all varying headers in cache key — use `Vary` header correctly
- Sanitize cache keys — don't include raw user input
- Invalidate user-specific caches on auth events (logout, role change, password reset)
- Redis: set `requirepass`, use TLS, bind to localhost or private network

## CDN Security

- Restrict origin to accept requests only from CDN IPs
- Enable WAF with OWASP Core Rule Set
- Use specific CORS origin allowlists, not wildcards
- Don't let CDN override application `Cache-Control` headers for sensitive endpoints

## Load Balancer Hardening

- Re-encrypt traffic between LB and backends (TLS to origin)
- Configure LB to **set** `X-Forwarded-For`, not append — prevents spoofing
- Set max request body size: nginx `client_max_body_size 10m;`
- Use TLS 1.2+ with strong cipher suites
- Patch for HTTP/2 rapid reset (CVE-2023-44487)

## Resource Exhaustion Prevention

- Set **timeouts** on every external call: connect 5s, read 30s, total 60s
- Add **maximum iteration limits** to all loops
- Set request body and file upload size limits
- Use `LIMIT` on every database query (max 100)
- Set connection pool limits: max 20 DB connections, idle timeout 30s
- Use regex libraries with backtracking limits (RE2) — prevent ReDoS
- Set server-level request timeout: `server.setTimeout(30000)`

## Queue & Message Broker Security

- Validate message schema before processing
- Configure dead-letter queues with max retry count (3-5)
- Set max message size limits
- Enable TLS and authentication for broker connections
- Set consumer concurrency limits to prevent resource exhaustion

## CSV/Excel Export Security

- **Sanitize all cell values** — prefix cells starting with `=`, `+`, `-`, `@`, `\t`, `\r` with single quote `'`
- Set entity expansion limits when processing uploaded XLSX (XML bomb prevention)
- Mask PII in exports — require additional auth for sensitive data exports
- Set max row/column limits when parsing uploaded CSV/Excel files
- Add `Content-Disposition: attachment` header on download endpoints
- Log export events for audit
